Rule 1 (single integer dim is within the valid range for the input tensor)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= if v_2 ≥ 0 then v_2 < ndim(v_1) else v_2 ≥ 0 - ndim(v_1)
>>
Rule 3 (each dim in the tuple is within the valid range for the input tensor)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tuple(int)} |= ∀i ∈ [0, v_2.len - 1] : if v_2[i] ≥ 0 then v_2[i] < ndim(v_1) else v_2[i] ≥ 0 - ndim(v_1)
>>
Rule 6 (tuple of dims is non-empty so shifts are defined)
{v_2 : tuple(int)} |= v_2.len > 0
>>
Rule 8 (number of specified dims does not exceed the tensor rank)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tuple(int)} |= v_2.len ≤ ndim(v_1)
